    "/Voice/v1/Numbers/order/change": {
      "post": {
        "tags": [
          "Orders"
        ],
        "summary": "Change an order.",
        "description": "Changes the telephone number(s) information by setting the values of the parameters passed.\n\nYou must pass the <code>x-customer-number</code> parameter in the header to complete this call successfully. For this endpoint, the <code>x-customer-number</code> is the same as your <strong>Child BusOrg</strong> ID or the BusOrg assigned to the billing account number (BAN).\n\nA change request can update the following information:\n- Subscriber name\n- Directory Listing (DL)\n- Customer Service Name (CSN)\n- Service address\n- Caller Name Delivery (CNAM)\n- E911 options\n\n__Note:__ Directory Listing (DL) and the E911 option is not supported for Local Inbound (LI) telephone numbers.\n\n<br>\n\n#### Local Inbound (LI) telephone numbers\n\nThe __orderMappingList__ array is a group of name-value pairs that are required based on the type of order you are changing. You can update the trunk group and route by using the name-value pair for __customerServiceName__ under the __orderMappingList__ object. See the example below.\n\n```\n\"orderMappingList\": [\n    {\n        \"attributeName\": \"customerServiceName\",\n        \"attributeValue\": \"1AB-CD-3\"\n    }\n  ]    \n```\n\n<br>\n\n#### Enhanced Local Service (ELS) telephone numbers\n\n__Required fields:__\n```\nproductID\nlnpIndicator\nsubscriberLineList\n```\n\nThe __orderMappingList__ array is a group of name-value pairs that are required based on the type of order you are changing. Below are the required fields for Directory Listing that you can include under the __orderMappingList__ object.\n\n```\n\"orderMappingList\": [\n    {\n        \"attributeName\": \"directoryListAction\",\n        \"attributeValue\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n        \"attributeName\": \"directoryListType\",\n        \"attributeValue\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n        \"attributeName\": \"directoryListType\",\n        \"attributeValue\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n        \"attributeName\": \"directoryFirstName\",\n        \"attributeValue\": \"\"\n    },\n                {\n        \"attributeName\": \"directoryLastName\",\n        \"attributeValue\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n        \"attributeName\": \"directoryBusinessName\",\n        \"attributeValue\": \"\"\n    }\n  ]    \n```\n",
        "operationId": "changeOrderUsingPOST",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "x-customer-number",
            "in": "header",
            "description": "customer number assigned by Lumen, also known as the BusOrg number.",
            "required": false,
            "style": "simple",
            "explode": false,
            "schema": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "example": "1-ABCDE"
          }
        ],
        "requestBody": {
          "description": "tnchangeRequest",
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/NewELSTNOrderRequest"
              }
            }
          },
          "required": true
        },
        "responses": {
          "202": {
            "description": "Accepted for processing.",
            "content": {
              "*/*": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/VoiceOrder"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "400": {
            "description": "Bad request."
          },
          "401": {
            "description": "You are not authorized to view the resource."
          },
          "402": {
            "description": "The resource you created does not meet the data requirement(s)."
          },
          "403": {
            "description": "Accessing the resource you were trying to reach is forbidden."
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "The resource you were trying to reach was not found."
          }
        },
        "deprecated": false,
        "security": [
          {
            "OAuth2": []
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "/Voice/v1/Numbers/order/disconnect": {
      "post": {
        "tags": [
          "Orders"
        ],
        "summary": "Disconnect telephone numbers.",
        "description": "Disconnects active service telephone numbers (a ported or new telephone number).\n\nYou must pass the <code>x-customer-number</code> parameter in the header to complete this call successfully. For this endpoint, the <code>x-customer-number</code> is the same as your <strong>Child BusOrg</strong> ID or the BusOrg assigned to the billing account number (BAN).\n\n__Required fields:__\n```\ncustomerRequestedDate\ntnList\n```\n\n__Note:__ The __customerRequestedDate__ must be set at least one business day in the future.\nLumen does not support CRD on weekends or Holidays\n",
        "operationId": "disconnectOrderUsingDELETE",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "x-customer-number",
            "in": "header",
            "description": "customer number assigned by Lumen, also known as the BusOrg number.",
            "required": false,
            "style": "simple",
            "explode": false,
            "schema": {
